<section id="find-your-model-by-flow-rate" class="my-10 not-prose">
  <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-navy mb-4">Find Your Model by Flow Rate</h2>
  <p class="text-text-light mb-3 max-w-3xl">
    Published model capacities vary by fluid, viscosity, temperature, and solids load. Use this as a first-pass selector, then confirm sizing with an application engineer.
  </p>
  <p class="text-text-light mb-5 max-w-3xl">
    DMPX and DMB models are Dolphin modules built around a remanufactured Alfa Laval centrifuge. The Alfa Laval base machine for every row is listed below, so a Dolphin module and the Alfa Laval model it is built on are always readable side by side. Dolphin is an independent remanufacturer and is not affiliated with or authorized by Alfa Laval.
  </p>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto border border-gray-100 rounded-xl shadow-sm">
    <table class="w-full text-sm text-left border-collapse">
      <thead>
        <tr class="bg-navy text-white">
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Flow rate (GPM)</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Model</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Alfa Laval base machine</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Self-clean or Manual</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Typical applications</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100 bg-white">
        {modelFlowRows.map((row) => (
          <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
            <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-navy whitespace-nowrap">{row.flow}</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">
              <a href={row.href} class="text-navy hover:text-gold transition-colors">{row.model}</a>
            </td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-text-light whitespace-nowrap">{row.base}</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-text-light whitespace-nowrap">{row.cleaning}</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-text-light">{row.applications}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>
